WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.803
-Hey, everybody. Welcome to
an all-new "Tonight Show."

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.605
We're here in New York City.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.673
It's a big nor'easter in 2021.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:09.809
And if you can see, the streets
are basically empty.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.144
I mean, the city
is kind of shut down right now.

00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:14.580
But we are going to do
a brand-new show for you guys

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.682
because we're here.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:18.218
But if this were
pre-pandemic times,

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:21.220
we would have to do the show
with no audience anyway.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.822
So with that in mind,

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:27.193
this might be the first normal
show we've done in 10 months.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.328
So let's do it!
Welcome to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:31.030
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:38.671
♪♪

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:46.312
♪♪

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.747
-From Rockefeller Center
in the heart of New York City,

00:00:48.747 --> 00:00:51.217
it's "The Tonight Show
Starring Jimmy Fallon."

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.053
Tonight, join Jimmy
and his guests --

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.824 line:0%
Musical guest Remi Wolf,

00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:00.493 line:0%
and featuring
the legendary Roots crew.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:03.963
And now here he is,
Jimmy Fallon.

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:09.269
♪♪

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:12.004
-Thank you very much!
Hello! Welcome! Thank you!

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:14.373
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:16.909
♪♪

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:19.078
Thank you very much, everybody.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:20.846
♪♪

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:22.348
Hello, welcome, welcome,

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.717
welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.452
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:01:26.452 --> 00:01:29.588
Thank you for watching at home.
I appreciate it.

00:01:29.588 --> 00:01:33.059
Well, guys, the first nor'easter
of 2021 began yesterday

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:35.094
and continued all day today,

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:37.497
just blasting
the Northeast with snow.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:40.566
Here in New York, a state
of emergency was declared.

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.468
I'm not really sure
that was necessary.

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:44.236
Since last March,
our resting status

00:01:44.236 --> 00:01:47.440
has pretty much been
state of emergency, but --

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.342
That's right, New York City
got nearly 2 feet of snow.

00:01:50.342 --> 00:01:52.211
All day, New Yorkers
were frantically shoveling

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:54.948
until they remembered
there's nowhere to go.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.583
But what a crazy storm
it's been so far --

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:59.486
freezing temperatures, high
winds, multiple feet of snow.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:02.055
Today, even the anti-maskers
were like, "Okay, give me one.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:04.090
Just -- Here --"

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.192
The weather is so bad,
tomorrow, Punxsutawney Phil

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:09.361
is gonna pop out of his little
groundhog Airbnb and be like,

00:02:09.361 --> 00:02:11.730
"What do you think
I'm predicting?

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.401
Go bother Sam Champion
with this crap."

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.970
Seriously, the weather
was so brutal,

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.238
even Joe Biden
spent the day at Mar-A-Lago.

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:20.706
[ Laughter, groaning ]

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:23.008
That's right.
The East Coast is being rocked

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:24.410
by a blizzard right now.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.546
In New York, it is so cold --

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.514
-How cold is it?

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:30.783
-It's so cold,
I saw a subway rat

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.219
wearing a pair
of Bernie mittens.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.687
It is so cold.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.389
-How cold is it?

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:38.223
-It's so cold,
Pfizer and Moderna

00:02:38.223 --> 00:02:40.826
are storing their vaccines
outside on Fifth Avenue.

00:02:40.826 --> 00:02:42.762
I mean, it is cold.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.630
-How cold is it?

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:48.067
-It's so cold, the New Year's
Eve ball went back up.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.102
It is so cold.

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:52.338
-No, Jimmy, stop.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.006
-What is it, Roots?

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:57.610
-When we say, "How cold is it?"
we mean it literally.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.246
We actually want to know
how cold it is.

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.380
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:04.250
-Oh, it's like 35 degrees.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.451
-Thank you.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.754
[ Applause ]

00:03:10.522 --> 00:03:12.691
-But the snowstorm
isn't bad news for everyone.

00:03:12.691 --> 00:03:15.261
Take a look at how one of
the pandas at the National Zoo

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:18.264
was handling it.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:31.344
Yeah, that panda either loves
the snow or is incredibly drunk.

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:32.678
30 seconds after this video,

00:03:32.678 --> 00:03:34.746
the panda threw up bamboo
for five straight minutes.

00:03:34.746 --> 00:03:35.815
They don't show that.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.283
Meanwhile, here in New York,

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:39.718
kids got some pretty mixed news
about schools this morning.

00:03:39.718 --> 00:03:40.753 line:0%
Listen to this.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:43.322 line:0%
-New York City schools
are closed.

00:03:43.322 --> 00:03:47.827 line:0%
However, students are required
to learn remotely today.

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:50.295
-Yeah, in the split-second
between hearing "schools closed"

00:03:50.295 --> 00:03:51.397
and "remote learning,"

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.932
every teacher finished
a bottle of wine.

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:54.266
Yeah.

00:03:54.266 --> 00:03:57.203
Come on. They made them
go to school on a snow day?

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:58.771
Seriously, those Zoom rooms
must've looked like

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.406
a pissed-off
"Brady Bunch" opening.

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:01.807
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.807 --> 00:04:03.742
Well, guys, today in Washington,
President Biden

00:04:03.742 --> 00:04:07.046 line:0%
met with 10 Republican senators
about their COVID relief plan.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.582 line:0%
They want about
$600 billion in aid,

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:12.518
while Democrats want
$1.9 trillion.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:14.119
Yeah, the meeting got heated.

00:04:14.119 --> 00:04:17.156
According to the transcript,
Biden shouted 12 "come on, mans"

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:20.259
and 19 "gimme a breaks."

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:22.295
Well, this isn't good. The
impeachment trial is next week,

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:25.064
and Trump's legal team
doesn't seem ready. Watch this.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:28.200 line:0%
-With just days to go until
his second impeachment trial,

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.369 line:0%
all five
of the impeachment lawyers

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:33.539 line:0%
expected to represent
former president Donald Trump

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:37.343 line:0%
have quit, splitting over
a disagreement in strategy.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:38.811
-Trump was furious.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:42.448
Not that they quit -- that he
couldn't fire them on Twitter.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.751
Yeah, Trump and his lawyers
disagreed on strategy.

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:49.188
Apparently, Trump got upset
when they wanted to have one.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.923
But there's good news for Trump,

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.424
because after he lost
five lawyers,

00:04:52.424 --> 00:04:54.660
he was able to replace them
with two new ones.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.062
Can we hear a little bit
about them?

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:58.497 line:0%
-Donald Trump has picked
two new attorneys,

00:04:58.497 --> 00:04:59.899
David Schoen and Bruce Castor.

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:02.401
-David Schoen was consulting
with Jeffrey Epstein

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:03.669
before his death.

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:06.472
Bruce Castor, most notably,
deciding not to go ahead

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:10.276
with the prosecution
against Bill Cosby in 2005.

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:12.578
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:16.149
-What? Was the guy who defended
Saddam Hussein not available?

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.950
I mean --

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:21.854
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:25.924
Even Rudy Giuliani thought,
"You're going with these guys?"

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:28.160
Listen to this. If you're still
traveling during the pandemic,

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.362
maybe this will give you
something else to think about.

00:05:30.362 --> 00:05:33.165 line:0%
-According to a safety
reporting system run by NASA,

00:05:33.165 --> 00:05:35.934 line:0%
the rise of in-flight errors
during commercial flights

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:41.073 line:0%
is being blamed on pilots being
rusty because of the pandemic.

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:43.142
-Don't worry.
It's just like riding a bike

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:45.511
30,000 feet above the ground.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:47.747
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:49.815
It's not good when you hear
a pilot walk into the cockpit

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:52.418
and go, "Oh, boy."

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:54.019
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.019 --> 00:05:57.723
"There's buttons on the
ceilings, too?" [ Babbles ]

00:05:57.723 --> 00:05:59.325
Some business news.
I saw that this month,

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:02.728
Dunkin' Donuts is offering
free coffee every Monday.

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:04.663
Well, in honor of that, we'd
like to give a little shout-out

00:06:04.663 --> 00:06:06.766
to their most loyal customer
in history.

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.668 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.759 line:0%
-♪ Yeah ♪

00:06:33.759 --> 00:06:35.928
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:37.296
-That's my dude.

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:41.033
I read about
a woman in Minnesota

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:43.435
who wanted to show her daughter
her wedding dress

00:06:43.435 --> 00:06:45.704
but had an interesting surprise.
Check this out.

00:06:45.704 --> 00:06:49.141 line:0%
-A Minnesota woman is on a quest
to find her wedding gown.

00:06:49.141 --> 00:06:50.843 line:0%
Wendy Taylor pulled out the box

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:53.912 line:0%
she paid to have professionally
packaged 14 years ago,

00:06:53.912 --> 00:06:55.381 line:0%
but she was was shocked to find

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:58.717 line:0%
her gown had been swapped
with someone else's.

00:06:58.717 --> 00:07:01.153
-Yeah. Then she opened
the frozen wedding cake

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:04.656
in the freezer
and discovered it was a burrito.

00:07:04.656 --> 00:07:06.492
The woman was like,
"This can't be my wedding dress

00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:08.561
because it doesn't
fit me at all."

00:07:08.561 --> 00:07:10.362
[ Laughter ]

00:07:10.362 --> 00:07:11.964
And finally,
I heard about a man in Idaho

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:15.367
who just won the lottery
for the sixth time.

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:18.170
Yeah, this last jackpot
was $250,000.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:20.873
And with the money,
he plans to buy Idaho.

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:25.177
Guys, I am so psyched that
Bryan Cranston is here tonight.

00:07:25.177 --> 00:07:29.014
We love Bryan Cranston.

00:07:29.014 --> 00:07:31.751
We were actually texting
over the weekend,

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:36.222
and it turns out that we're both
obsessed with fancy soaps.

00:07:36.222 --> 00:07:38.057
Yeah, here, check this out.

00:07:38.057 --> 00:07:40.059
♪♪

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:42.261
-♪ Fancy soaps in a fancy dish ♪

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:44.463
♪ One's a seashell,
one's a fish ♪

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:46.699
♪ One soap's purple,
one soap's teal ♪

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:48.901
♪ One soap's made
with dry oatmeal ♪

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:51.003
-♪ Lavender, lemongrass,
lily, lilac ♪

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:53.205
♪ This one comes
in a drawstring sack ♪

00:07:53.205 --> 00:07:55.341
♪ Tiny soaps, vanilla and plum ♪

00:07:55.341 --> 00:07:57.509
-♪ Put them out
when company comes ♪

00:07:57.509 --> 00:07:59.812
-♪ Soaps were made
to make you cleaner ♪

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:01.947
-♪ This one's citrus,
that's verbena ♪

00:08:01.947 --> 00:08:04.083
-♪ Heart-shaped soaps
for a love that's true ♪

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:06.252
-♪ Crystal soap
you can see right through ♪

00:08:06.252 --> 00:08:08.387
♪ Dish, terrine, platter, tray ♪

00:08:08.387 --> 00:08:10.623
♪ Fancy soaps go on display ♪

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:12.825
-♪ Pine tree soap
to put in your pocket ♪

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:14.960
-♪ Goat milk soap
from the farmer's market ♪

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:16.795
-♪ Tea time soap
with chamomile ♪

00:08:16.795 --> 00:08:19.264
-♪ Shea butter soap
for a softer feel ♪

00:08:19.264 --> 00:08:21.500
-♪ Fruity soaps
smell like fruit snacks ♪

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.468
-♪ Lava soap
that's entirely black ♪

00:08:23.468 --> 00:08:25.637
-♪ When a friend stops by
whether ready or not ♪

00:08:25.637 --> 00:08:27.906
♪ No liquid soap
for a two-pump shot ♪

00:08:27.906 --> 00:08:30.042
♪ Not potpourri
nor candlesticks ♪

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:33.245
♪ Just fancy soaps
in a fancy dish ♪

00:08:33.245 --> 00:08:35.447
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:35.447 --> 00:08:36.716
-My thanks to Bryan Cranston!

